    <statement><p>Find the solution to the differential equation
<me>\frac{dy}{dt} = 0.3 (y - 200)</me>
if <m>y=35</m> when <m>t=0</m>.</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-165e^{0.3t}+200</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int\frac{dy}{y-200} = \int 0.3 dt,</me>
so
<me>\ln|y-200| = 0.3 t +C.</me>
Solving for <m>y</m>,
<me>y = 200 + A e^{0.3 t},</me>
where <m>A = \pm e^C</m>.
The initial condition, <m>y(0)=35</m>, gives
<m>35 = 200 + A</m>, so <m>A = 165</m>, and 
<me>y= 200 - 165 e^{0.3 t}.</me>



</solution>
